 "verdict": "dead",
 "notes": "Implemented as specified: fixed-clock west_short 03:00->10:00 ET short with 0.6% stop, gap>1% skip, macro0830 force-flat at 08:32 (never a look-ahead skip); fix-anchored pmfix_fade/amfix_fade/pmfix_momo use the Europe/London 15:00/10:30 auction clock converted to ET per date (35 sessions per 2025-26 shift by one hour); ny_long 10:05->16:30. MAIN west_short +$5,062 / PF 1.11 on 437 trades is a 2026 artefact: 2025 alone PF 0.87 (-$2,798), one day (2026-03-03, +$2,889) is 57% of the net, PF 1.05 without it, median trade -$42, top-10 trades = 269% of net; PRIOR PF 0.83 (-$3,199); 2015-2024 PF 0.90-0.91 with 8 losing years of 10. Walk-forward OOS 2023-2026 PF 0.96 (-$1,448, 497 trades); OOS 2025-26 PF 0.997 (-$76, 289 trades) -> below the 1.03 bar. Lucid on the OOS stream: best 5 micros, exp_net_lb -$146, point estimate +$78 vs zero-edge control +$95, not recommended. All 24 grid cells have exp_net_lb -$146 on both periods. The fix legs are dead post-2015 as expected (pmfix_fade/amfix_fade/pmfix_momo PF 0.51-0.91 in 2015-2024); their small 2025-26 positives (PF 1.03-1.13, one day = 150-360% of net for pmfix_fade/pmfix_momo) are noise. ny_long is NEGATIVE on the gold bull tape (MAIN PF 0.95, -$1,822; buy-and-hold 10:05-16:30 on the same 422 days gross -$2,059 = 0.16 bp/day) while the overnight 17:00->03:00 return of the same days was +$18,471 (11.6 bp/day): gold's 2025-26 drift accrued entirely outside the daytime windows. By-product kept: the 30-min clock profile 2020-2026 (results/cal_gold_clock/clock_profile_30min.csv): west 03:00-10:00 -0.4 bp/day with the only significant slots 05:00 (-0.66 bp, t -2.1), 09:30 (-0.92 bp) and 16:30 (-0.60 bp, t -2.5); Asia 18:00-02:00 +5.7 bp/day. Filter statement for the MGC ORB / mean-reversion legs: the daytime 03:00-10:00 window carries no positive drift, so no long-bias assumption there; the 16:30-17:00 slot is reliably negative (do not hold gold longs into the 17:00 close).",
